      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`convrot_int8`'s comfy_kitchen backend splits tall GEMMs into 8192-row calls (`SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS`) to keep them off comfy_kitchen's Stream-K schedule. Every extra call also copies its slice of the output, and with comfy-kitchen 0.2.37 whole-model runs are faster unsplit on every GPU we measured.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Default `SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS` to `0` (one call per layer). A positive value still splits.\n- Update the comment in `convrot_int8_comfy_kitchen.py`, `environment_variables.mdx` and `quantization.mdx`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nSplitting rows does not change any row's arithmetic. Outputs are bit-identical with and without the split (same-input ablation on all three GPUs).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nMiniMax-H3 pruned INT8 checkpoint, comfy_kitchen backend, SGLD ComfyUI workflow, 4 steps × 3 seeds. Steady model-time gain going from rows 8192 to 0:\n\n| GPU | 480p / 124 frames | 768p / 124 frames | Ref2VA / 4 refs |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| RTX 4090 | +3.91% | +2.40% | +2.14% |\n| RTX 5090 | +2.96% | +1.62% | +1.26% |\n| H200 (kitchen forced) | +2.20% | +1.56% | +1.48% |\n\nH200, B200 and RTX 5090 default to the JIT backend, which does not use this setting. RTX 4090 (sm89) always uses comfy_kitchen.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38672290126](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38672290126)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38672290191](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38672290191)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38672289965](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38672289965)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
