  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 3,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2/docs%2Fdocs%2Fsglang-diffusion%2Fenvironment_variables.mdx",
      "changes": 6,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Fsglang-diffusion%2Fenvironment_variables.mdx?ref=2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2",
      "deletions": 3,
      "filename": "docs/docs/sglang-diffusion/environment_variables.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -110,13 +110,13 @@ description: \"Configure SGLang diffusion behavior with environment variables.\"\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n       <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", fontWeight: 500, backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}><code>SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS</code></td>\n-      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}><code>8192</code></td>\n-      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>Max activation rows per <code>convrot_int8</code> fused GEMM on the <code>comfy_kitchen</code> backend. Set <code>0</code> to disable row splitting.</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}><code>0</code></td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>Max activation rows per <code>convrot_int8</code> fused GEMM on the <code>comfy_kitchen</code> backend. <code>0</code> (default) issues one call; a positive value splits large-M GEMMs by rows.</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n       <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", fontWeight: 500, backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}><code>SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MIN_SPLIT_N</code></td>\n       <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}><code>8192</code></td>\n-      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>Minimum output features before <code>convrot_int8</code> (<code>comfy_kitchen</code> backend) splits large-M GEMMs. Narrow outputs stay as a single call.</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>Minimum output features before <code>convrot_int8</code> (<code>comfy_kitchen</code> backend) splits large-M GEMMs when <code>SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS</code> is positive. Narrow outputs stay as a single call.</td>\n     </tr>\n   </tbody>\n </table>",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2/docs%2Fdocs%2Fsglang-diffusion%2Fenvironment_variables.mdx",
      "sha": "cbcb93c3b46e9e0a2b976fb9b65545f85228c979",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 6,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2/docs%2Fdocs%2Fsglang-diffusion%2Fquantization.mdx",
      "changes": 10,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Fsglang-diffusion%2Fquantization.mdx?ref=2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2",
      "deletions": 4,
      "filename": "docs/docs/sglang-diffusion/quantization.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -498,10 +498,12 @@ for the 24 GB offload recipe, including why `vae` must stay out of\n `--layerwise-offload-components`.\n </Warning>\n \n-With the `comfy_kitchen` backend, large-M GEMMs (`rows > 8192` and\n-`out_features >= 8192`) are split by rows so the fused kernel stays on the\n-data-parallel CUTLASS config. Override the thresholds with\n-`SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS` and `SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MIN_SPLIT_N`.\n+With the `comfy_kitchen` backend, each GEMM is one fused call by default.\n+`SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS=N` splits large-M GEMMs (`rows > N` and\n+`out_features >= SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MIN_SPLIT_N`, default 8192) into N-row\n+calls, which keeps them on comfy_kitchen's data-parallel CUTLASS config; on\n+MiniMax-H3 with comfy-kitchen 0.2.37 the extra calls and output copies cost more\n+than they save.\n \n ### Skipping Layers\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2/docs%2Fdocs%2Fsglang-diffusion%2Fquantization.mdx",
      "sha": "e2de3bcb35f503aead3990133aa098f9da6fbeef",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 5,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2/python%2Fsglang%2Fmultimodal_gen%2Fruntime%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fconvrot_int8_comfy_kitchen.py",
      "changes": 15,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fsglang%2Fmultimodal_gen%2Fruntime%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fconvrot_int8_comfy_kitchen.py?ref=2763beb4584791a80e1a5547e5a54a82fc02ebb2",
      "deletions": 10,
      "filename": "python/sglang/multimodal_gen/runtime/layers/quantization/convrot_int8_comfy_kitchen.py",
      "patch": "@@ -35,16 +35,11 @@\n # comfy_kitchen's dtype codes for the fused op's output.\n _OUT_DTYPE_CODE = {torch.float32: 0, torch.float16: 1, torch.bfloat16: 2}\n \n-# comfy_kitchen picks its CUTLASS tile configuration from a threshold tree\n-# (select_fused_int8_config in cutlass_gemm_int8.cu). Shapes whose N falls under\n-# its 24832 cutoff but whose M is large get a Stream-K schedule, which exists to\n-# balance load when there are too few tiles to fill the GPU. At H3's 32700 tokens\n-# qkv_proj already launches ~21k CTAs over the 4090's 128 SMs, so Stream-K's\n-# workspace and fixup reduction are pure overhead: 26.5 ms against 17.9 ms for\n-# the identical tile without it. Capping rows per call keeps the plain\n-# data-parallel config, and is bit-exact because splitting rows does not change\n-# any single row's arithmetic.\n-_MAX_ROWS_PER_CALL = int(os.environ.get(\"SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS\", \"8192\"))\n+# Rows per comfy_kitchen int8_linear call; 0 issues one call. Splitting keeps tall,\n+# narrow-N GEMMs off comfy_kitchen's Stream-K schedule, but every extra call also\n+# copies its slice of the output, and whole-model MiniMax-H3 runs (comfy-kitchen\n+# 0.2.37, pruned INT8) are 1.3-3.9% faster unsplit on RTX 4090, RTX 5090 and H200.\n+_MAX_ROWS_PER_CALL = int(os.environ.get(\"SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MAX_ROWS\", \"0\"))\n # Narrow outputs do not recover the cost of writing results back through a\n # preallocated buffer; H3's out_proj and fc2 (N=5376) both measure slower split.\n _MIN_SPLIT_OUTPUT = int(os.environ.get(\"SGLANG_KITCHEN_INT8_MIN_SPLIT_N\", \"8192\"))",
